After the defeat of [[Calamity Ganon]], Robbie moved to the [[Hateno Ancient Tech Lab]], where he lead the development of the [[Purah Pad]].<ref name="Profile">{{Cite|An engineer whose eccentric style adds a lot to his reputation as a wild genius.<br/><br/>He once helped Link from his research facility at the Akkala Ancient Tech Lab. Since then, he's moved to the Hateno Ancient Tech Lab to help Purah develop the Purah Pad. Robbie thinks he did much of the work on the device, so he's a bit grumbly that it's not named after him.|Character Profiles|TotK}}</ref> Due to the amount of work that he contributed, Robbie is upset that it was named after [[Purah]] instead of himself.<ref name="Profile"/> Since the start of the [[Upheaval]], he and [[Jerrin]] have resided in [[Lookout Landing]].{{Fact}}

[[File:TotK Robbie Introduction.png|thumb|left|250px|alt= A screenshot of Robbie appearing shocked inside Lookout Landing. Text on-screen displays his name, along with the title "Head of Purah Pad Development".|Robbie's introduction]]
When [[Link]] first arrives in Lookout Landing, Robbie can be found inspecting the broken pieces of his [[Hot-Air Balloon]]. As Link approaches, he will recognize the sound of his footsteps as he approaches him.<ref>{{Cite|Ah, what a pleasant morning!|Robbie|TotK}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Those footsteps...|Robbie|TotK}}</ref> At first, he comments on the day's [[Weather]].<ref>{{Cite|Ah, what a fine afternoon!|Robbie|TotK}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Ah, what an excellent night!|Robbie|TotK}}</ref> When he realizes he is speaking to Link, he confronts him and asks where he has been.<ref>{{Cite|Hey. Hey, YOU! Where have you been?!|Robbie|TotK}}</ref> However, he tells Link not to answer, instead instructing him to meet with Purah at the [[Research Lab]], claiming she has been worried ever since he and [[Princess Zelda|Zelda]] disappeared.<ref>{{Cite|Don't answer that. Tell me later. For now, you should hurry and go talk to {{Color TotK|Red|Purah}}. She's been in a tizzy ever since you and the princess disappeared. She's in the building with the telescope, up on the {{Color TotK|Red|second floor}}. Go see her and give her some peace of mind, will ya?|Robbie|TotK}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Hey. You! I told you—talk to me later. For now you should hurry up and go to {{Color TotK|Red|Purah}}. She's in the building with the telescope, up on the {{Color TotK|Red|second floor}}. Go see her and give her some peace of mind, will ya?|Robbie|TotK}}</ref>

After Link has started "[[Crisis at Hyrule Castle]]", Robbie will yell at Link about how worried they have been since he went missing.<ref>{{Cite|Hey, you! Do you have any idea how worried we've been?!|Robbie|TotK}}</ref> He also notices Link's new [[Right Arm]], claiming he overheard Purah discussing it.<ref>{{Cite|So that's the arm, huh? I...overheard Purah talking about it. Hmmm. I...see. Yeah, it's pretty weird, all right.|Robbie|TotK}}</ref> Since Link has the Purah Pad, Robbie informs him that it is capable of being upgraded.<ref>{{Cite|Hmmm... Nope, now's not the time for distractions! That's got to wait until later. Anyway, I hear you've got yourself the {{Color TotK|Red|Purah Pad}} now. You know, that Purah Pad of yours can get a lot more powerful. I know its real potential.|Robbie|TotK}}</ref> However, he wants to help [[Josha]] with her [[Chasm Research]] before he continues with its development.<ref>{{Cite|I've got big plans for that device, but first I need to help Josha with her {{Color TotK|Red|investigations into the Depths}}.|Robbie|TotK}}</ref> He invites Link to meet him at the Hateno Ancient Tech Lab after he is finished.<ref>{{Cite|But then—oh, yes, THEN!—I will head back to the {{Color TotK|Red|lab in Hateno Village}} to resume my research. So, once I'm able to finish up here, you should join me there!|Robbie|TotK}}</ref>

